+As the stack pointer swapping mechanism relies upon the fact,
+that stack pointers are conventionally 128b aligned,
+an illegal instruction exception shall be raised
+if the execution of any instructions of this extension is attempted
+when the `x2` is not 128b aligned.
+
 Software can deactivate the stack pointer swap mechanism
 by writing zero to {xsp}.`PUSH`.
 
